  "qualification": "Nine shared public BRep groups, one internal duplicate/gap rejection and one public IO boundary group extend the corpus. BRep/IO release suites pass 718 all-feature and 710 minimal-feature tests. Both affected all-target strict Clippy configurations, warning-denied rustdoc, fuzz-target compilation and formatting pass. Source-path consumers execute 23 preserved groups on the baseline and 33 on the candidate; actual zero-import WASM executes all 33 candidate groups. This is the affected boundary corpus, not a rerun of the entire prior 253-group WASM inventory. All 654 historical native archives re-encode byte-identically; 159 STEP files import 173 bodies and replay. The 829-file historical inventory has 420 distinct contents; text controls are inventory-only. All 49 fresh baseline/candidate native pairs are byte-identical. 22 new solid archive files (13 distinct contents) repeat deterministically and cold-replay. No scalar encoding or schema migration is introduced.",
  "costs": "Three alternating pairs cover 12 preserved completed workflows and three absolute processes cover two new construction/replay workflows, each with a first call and three repeated fresh-input calls. All 21 processes pass their assertions. The 24 matched phase ratios range 0.819853 to 1.030648; 0 exceed the 10% review marker and 3 increase allocation calls or requested bytes. All adverse samples, RSS and binary/artifact sizes are retained. Instrumented shared-host samples establish neither a general speedup nor internal work/heap bounds. The complete new selected-cap recipe takes 9.150s on its first call and 8.868s per repeated call, with 9.456/9.460 GB of cumulative requested allocation respectively. Peak process RSS across all trials is 23.57 MiB. Requested allocation is traffic, not simultaneous live memory. This expensive recipe and the 1158.4s repeated archive comparison remain explicit resource follow-ups; no cause or optimization is established.",
  "limits": "Only complete-turn shells from simple, strictly positive-radius profiles with replayable scalar charts and a common similarity-projectable meridian plane are added. Exact procedural metrics can remain unavailable. General curved solid Booleans, partial/axis-touching revolutions, independent selected angular/axial fields, arbitrary affine transport, procedural STEP, whole-operation work/heap/coefficient/cancellation bounds, runtime fuzz/ASan/lexicase, formal coverage, MSRV, installed distributions and production binding gates remain open. All 28 work packages remain open/in-progress. Full pre-push qualification remains required; the consumed eaa0 one-time exception does not authorize publishing this increment.",
